<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="chin-noodle" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Chinese Noodle Soup</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell><term>Broth:</term></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>8 to 10 cups chicken broth</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>4 garlic cloves, smashed</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>1" piece of ginger, sliced</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 teaspoons soy sauce</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 teaspoons chinese cooking wine or mirin</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>4 teaspoons honey</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon sesame oil</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><term>Toppings &amp; Noodles</term></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>6 oz chinese egg noodles</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 large bok choy</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>Other vegetables (e.g. green onions, carrots, broccoli, bean sprouts, zucchini, cabbage)</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>1 \frac{1}{2}</m> pounds chicken</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Place broth ingredients and carrots in a saucepan over high heat.  Place lid on, bring to simmer then reduce to medium high.  Simmer for 10 minutes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          At the same time, prepare noodles.  Use sesame oil to prevent clumping.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Chop vegetables, remove garlic and ginger, and cook vegetables in broth (slow-cooking vegetables go in first).  Cook bok choy last (1 minute).
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Place noodles in bowls, and pour soup over noodles.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          I suggest not boiling all the noodles at once.  Just boil enough for each meal.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>